// Phase 3 (INTER), GLOBAL MOTION entropy sync. A REAL single-ref
// (REFERENCE_MODE SINGLE) frame with a NON-IDENTITY (ROTZOOM) global-motion
// model where aomenc chose GLOBALMV for several blocks. HarborInterFrameWalk
// must resolve the per-block global MV (HarborGlobalMv) + the ref-mv-stack
// global candidates + the GLOBALMV-nontranslational motion_mode suppression and
// stay od_ec-bit-exact vs the SW oracle symbol-by-symbol to frame
// end. The stream is a synthetic strong pan/zoom source encoded with aomenc
// 3.12.1 (--enable-global-motion=1). The target frame (index 3) is all-inter
// with gmType[LAST]/[LAST2]=ROTZOOM and 2 GLOBALMV blocks (positions (0,0) and
// (8,8)) with non-zero position-dependent global MVs, plus 5 NEAREST blocks
// whose ref-mv stacks are populated by those global candidates. Block (8,8)
// exercises the non-translational-global motion_mode suppression. The residual
// uses only supported tx sizes (TX_4X16, TX_8X32).

// Goldens captured from the SW TileDecoder decode of the embedded gm OBU:
// the packed HW inputs (CDF banks, TMVP field, gm params, header flags) and the
// SW od_ec per-symbol rng trace + GLOBALMV block list.
